# Every runtime variable this app reads, with placeholders only. Never a real value.
# Copy to .env for local work. .env is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# App Store note: for a code-defaults app the operator Environment Variables tab is
# EMPTY. Platform-injected variables arrive at the pod level. Anything typed into the
# tab is an override and a liability.

# --- Runtime contract (platform-injected; do not set in the Dockerfile) ---
# PORT is read at runtime, default 8080, bound 0.0.0.0. Leave unset locally.
# PORT=

# --- Storage (the file-storage add-on injects STORAGE_MOUNT_PATH=/data) ---
# Resolution order: DATA_DIR, then STORAGE_MOUNT_PATH, then an absolute local default.
# DATA_DIR=
# STORAGE_MOUNT_PATH=

# --- Access control (server-side only; never reaches the browser) ---
# WRITES ARE CLOSED BY DEFAULT. With neither variable below set, every write route
# returns 401 while reads, health, and diagnostics stay open. That is deliberate: an
# absent token is the container default and this tab is meant to be empty, so treating
# "no token" as "open" would put an unauthenticated write endpoint on a public ingress
# by omission.
#
# To host for a team, set BOTH of these. The token must be at least 24 characters, and
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN is mandatory alongside it; a wildcard origin makes the app refuse to
# start whether or not a token is set.
# ENLIGHTENMENT_TEAM_TOKEN=
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN=https://enlightenment.apps.bluestaq.com

# To allow anonymous writes for single-user LOCAL work only, set this to 1. It cannot be
# combined with a team token: the app refuses to start on the contradiction. Never set
# this on a hosted deployment.
# ENLIGHTENMENT_ALLOW_ANONYMOUS=

# --- Build identity (stamped by CI; falls back to the package version) ---
# BUILD_ID=
